cord with no session is sent under its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record identifier. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The record’s vendor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties (","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the like).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":" or is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":" and one holding a value JSON can’t."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"